IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`

-- Israel: the rules of reading in the Interpretation Law 5741-1981: ss 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9 and 25.
--
-- Each rule is a function over a small typed representation of what the rule operates on. The rule extends the
-- meaning of a word of another enactment; it does not change a fact, so the facts it needs are the ones a witness
-- could state about the word in front of them (which grammatical number it is written in, what kind of body it
-- names). Every one of these rules is subject to s 1's gate: the Law applies only if no other provision deals with
-- the matter and nothing in the matter or its context is inconsistent with it. When the gate fails the rule REFUSES
-- (il-interpretation-gate.l4), because the Law then does not say what the words mean.
-- FALSE, in the functions below, always means "this rule of the Law does not extend the word to that case".
--
-- Source: the unofficial Wikisource consolidation, ../../source/law.wiki (src:N). English glosses are mine; the Hebrew governs.

§ `Interpretation Law: the rules of reading (ss 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 25)`

§§ `Nouns`

-- s 2
DECLARE `Where a defined term is used` IS ONE OF
    `in the enactment that defines it`
    `in regulations made under the enactment that defines it`
    `in some other enactment`

DECLARE `The form a defined term takes` IS ONE OF
    `the term itself`
    `a grammatical form derived from the term`

DECLARE `A use of a defined term` HAS
    `where it is used`                                                          IS A `Where a defined term is used`
    `the form it takes`                                                         IS A `The form a defined term takes`
    `another provision deals with the matter`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4
DECLARE `What a provision speaks of when it speaks of a person` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a corporation`
    `a body of persons that is not a corporation`
    `a thing that is neither a person nor a body of persons`

-- s 5
DECLARE `Grammatical number` IS ONE OF
    `the singular`
    `the plural`

-- s 6
DECLARE `Grammatical gender` IS ONE OF
    `the masculine`
    `the feminine`

-- s 7
DECLARE `A general word that follows a list` HAS
    `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is "or"`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is "other"`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an expression like them`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is accompanied by "similar"`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is accompanied by "of like kind"`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `How a general word is read against the list before it` IS ONE OF
    `apart from the list: it does not take its sense from the list`
    `by analogy to the list`

-- s 9
DECLARE `What an act is done according to` IS ONE OF
    `the enactment itself`
    `regulations made under the enactment`
    `some other instrument`

DECLARE `A use of "according to"` HAS
    `the expression is "according to" or one like it`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `what the act is done according to`                  IS A `What an act is done according to`

-- s 25
DECLARE `A version of an enactment's wording` HAS
    `in force from`  IS A DATE
    `wording`        IS A STRING

DECLARE `An enactment that another enactment refers to` HAS
    `its versions`                                                 IS A LIST OF `A version of an enactment's wording`
    `provisions of another enactment took its place from`          IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `What a reference to an enactment reaches` HAS
    `the wording in force on the day it is resorted to`   IS A MAYBE `A version of an enactment's wording`
    `the provisions that came in its place in another enactment`  IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Named refusals`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 7 speaks only of the words "or" and "other" and expressions like them` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 7 speaks only of the words \"or\" and \"other\" and expressions like them"

§§ `s 2 — a defined term bears its definition`

-- src:25 | מונח שהוגדר בחיקוק – משמעו כהגדרתו, והגדרה זו תחול גם על תקנות שהותקנו לפי אותו חיקוק, וכל צורה דקדוקית הנגזרת מהמונח תתפרש לפי אותה משמעות, הכל אם אין הוראה אחרת לענין הנדון ואם אין בענין הנדון או בהקשרו דבר שאינו מתיישב עם אותה הגדרה.
@ref Interpretation Law s 2 (src:25)
GIVEN use IS A `A use of a defined term`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 — the defined term bears its definition in` use `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (       (use's `where it is used` EQUALS `in the enactment that defines it`
              OR use's `where it is used` EQUALS `in regulations made under the enactment that defines it`)
            AND NOT use's `another provision deals with the matter`
            AND NOT use's `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition`)

§§ `s 4 — a person includes a body of persons`

-- src:65 | מקום שמדובר באדם – אף חבר־בני־אדם במשמע, בין שהוא תאגיד ובין שאינו תאגיד.
@ref Interpretation Law s 4 (src:65)
GIVEN subject IS A `What a provision speaks of when it speaks of a person`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 — a reference to a person reaches` subject `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER subject
         WHEN `a natural person`                                   THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a corporation`                                      THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a body of persons that is not a corporation`        THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a thing that is neither a person nor a body of persons` THEN FALSE)

§§ `s 5 — singular and plural`

-- src:68 | האמור בלשון יחיד – אף לשון רבים במשמע, וכן להיפך.
@ref Interpretation Law s 5 (src:68)
GIVEN written IS A `Grammatical number`
      asked IS A `Grammatical number`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5 — what is said in` written `reaches` asked `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER written
         WHEN `the singular` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the plural`   THEN TRUE)

§§ `s 6 — masculine and feminine`

-- src:71 | האמור בלשון זכר – אף לשון נקבה במשמע, וכן להיפך.
@ref Interpretation Law s 6 (src:71)
GIVEN written IS A `Grammatical gender`
      asked IS A `Grammatical gender`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6 — what is said in` written `reaches` asked `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER written
         WHEN `the masculine` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the feminine`  THEN TRUE)

§§ `s 7 — "or" and "other" do not infer from the list`

-- src:74 | המלים ”או“, ”אחר“ או ביטוי דומה להן – להבדיל מן המפורט שלפניהן הן באות ולא להקיש לו, זולת אם יש עמן המלים ”דומה“ או ”כיוצא בזה“ או ביטוי אחר שמשמעו היקש.
@ref Interpretation Law s 7 (src:74)
GIVEN matter IS A `The matter in question`
      word IS A `A general word that follows a list`
GIVETH A `How a general word is read against the list before it`
`s 7 — how the general word is read against the list before it, for` matter `:` word MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   (   word's `it is "or", "other" or an expression like them`
               OR word's `it is "or"`
               OR word's `it is "other"`
               OR word's `it is an expression like them`)
         THEN IF   (   word's `it is accompanied by "similar", "of like kind" or another expression of analogy`
                    OR word's `it is accompanied by "similar"`
                    OR word's `it is accompanied by "of like kind"`
                    OR word's `it is accompanied by another expression of analogy`)
              THEN `by analogy to the list`
              ELSE `apart from the list: it does not take its sense from the list`
         ELSE `s 7 speaks only of the words "or" and "other" and expressions like them`)

§§ `s 9 — "according to"`

-- src:80 | הביטוי ”לפי“, לענין חיקוק פלוני, או ביטוי כיוצא בו – משמעו גם לפי תקנות שהותקנו מכוחו של החיקוק.
@ref Interpretation Law s 9 (src:80)
GIVEN use IS A `A use of "according to"`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9 — "according to" an enactment reaches an act done according to` use `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (    use's `the expression is "according to" or one like it`
         AND (   use's `what the act is done according to` EQUALS `the enactment itself`
              OR use's `what the act is done according to` EQUALS `regulations made under the enactment`))

§§ `s 25 — a reference to an enactment`

-- src:139 | אזכור של חיקוק בחיקוק אחר – כוונתו לחיקוק המאוזכר כנוסחו בשעה שנזקקים לו, לרבות הוראות שנוספו בו והוראות שבאו במקומו בחיקוק אחר.
@ref Interpretation Law s 25 (src:139)
-- The version of an enactment's wording that a reference reaches: the one in force on the day the reference is
-- resorted to, "including provisions added to it", which a later version contains. NOTHING when no version was
-- in force that day (the enactment had no wording to be resorted to).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      versions IS A LIST OF `A version of an enactment's wording`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A version of an enactment's wording`
`s 25 — the wording in force on` day `among` versions MEANS
    foldl pick NOTHING versions
    WHERE
        pick best v MEANS
            IF   v's `in force from` AT MOST day
            THEN CONSIDER best
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST v
                 WHEN JUST b  THEN IF v's `in force from` ABOVE b's `in force from` THEN JUST v ELSE best
            ELSE best

@ref Interpretation Law s 25 (src:139)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
      referred IS AN `An enactment that another enactment refers to`
GIVETH A `What a reference to an enactment reaches`
`s 25 — what a reference to an enactment reaches when it is resorted to on` day `, for` matter `:` referred MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (`What a reference to an enactment reaches` WITH
            `the wording in force on the day it is resorted to` IS `s 25 — the wording in force on` day `among` (referred's `its versions`)
            `the provisions that came in its place in another enactment` IS
                CONSIDER referred's `provisions of another enactment took its place from`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                WHEN JUST from THEN from AT MOST day)

-- Law s 25 speaks of "a reference to an enactment in another enactment". A reference made in an enactment is within it; a reference made in a
-- private contract or any other document is not. s 1 applies the Law to administrative directions too, but s 25's own words say "another
-- enactment", so whether a reference in an administrative direction is within s 25 is not answered: the rule refuses (F37).
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 25 speaks of a reference in another enactment; whether a reference in an administrative direction is within it is not said` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 25 speaks of a reference to an enactment in another enactment; s 1 applies the Law to administrative directions, but nothing says whether a reference made in an administrative direction is within s 25"

-- src:139 | אזכור של חיקוק בחיקוק אחר – כוונתו לחיקוק המאוזכר כנוסחו בשעה שנזקקים לו, לרבות הוראות שנוספו בו והוראות שבאו במקומו בחיקוק אחר.
@ref Interpretation Law s 25 (the kind of instrument that refers) (src:139)
GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of instrument`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25 — a reference to an enactment made in an instrument of the kind` kind `is within s 25, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `the instrument is an enactment`                THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the instrument is an administrative direction` THEN `s 25 speaks of a reference in another enactment; whether a reference in an administrative direction is within it is not said`
         WHEN `the instrument is a private contract`          THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the instrument is some other document`         THEN FALSE)
